        "nonzero_rank_defects_verified": true,
        "source_caveat": "Statements 8--9 of arXiv:2306.16400 assert that an abelian intersection N normal in both support groups yields the quasi-abelian/zero-defect reduction.  Their proof assumes without justification that the extensions by N split.  Here G_a=C16 is a nonsplit extension of N=C8 by C2, and the direct matrix ranks give delta_X=delta_Z=2.  Thus the row is a counterexample to the zero-defect statement as written; a split-extension hypothesis repairs the application."
      },
